===Proper noun===
{{en-prop}}

# The official [[language]] of [[Turkey]], [[Republic of Cyprus]] (alongside [[Greek]]) and [[Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus]].
#: {{syn|en|Anatolian Turkish}}
# {{syn of|en|Turkic}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=A Century of British Orientalists, 1902-2001|page=97|editor={{w|Clifford Edmund Bosworth|C. Edmund Bosworth}}|year=2001|passage=This dictionary for Chaghatay '''Turkish''' (although it also contains much material for what the author calls 'Rūmī', i.e. south-western Turkish, above all, Ottoman) is the Sanglakh of an obscure eighteenth-century compiler}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Culture and Learning in Islam|page=256|author=Ekmeleddin İhsanoğlu|year=2003|passage=M.A. Òerbak considers Chaghatay '''Turkish''' a period of Uzbek.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=A Millennium of Turkish Literature|page=6|author=Talat S. Halman, Jayne L. Warner|year=2011|passage=[...] these works include stories of the battles the Turks fought against the Chinese, a variety of legends, and numerous specimens of verse (found mostly in Chinese translation) written in Uyghur '''Turkish'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Possessed|author=Elif Batuman|year=2011|passage=And my uncle always shouted: “Uzbek '''Turkish''' is very close to our Turkish language!”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=In the Shadow of the Gods: The Emperor in World History|author=Dominic Lieven|year=2022|passage=It was Navai who through his poetry almost single-handedly turned his native Chaghatay '''Turkish''' into a literary language.}}

