===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Of, from, or pertaining to Turkey, the Turkish people or the Turkish language.
#: {{syn|en|Anatolian Turkish}}
#* {{quote-book|en|url=https://books.google.com.tr/books?id=tXlSDwAAQBAJ&pg=PT410&dq=%22+put+on+a+mysterious%22|title=Higher Lessons in English: A work on English Grammar and composition|author=Kellogg et al|publisher=Prabhat Prakashan|date=2021-01-19|passage=When a question was asked, would put on a mysterious look. Shake his head. Smoke in silence. Observe, at length, he had doubts. Presided at the council, in state. Swayed a '''Turkish''' pipe instead of a scepter. Known to sit with eyes closed ...{{...}}}}
# {{syn of|en|Turkic}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1962|title=Turkish and Mongolian Studies|page=37|author={{w|Gerard Clauson}}|passage=[...] in Mongolian and some '''Turkish''' languages}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Chuvash Studies|page=119|author=András Róna-Tas|year=1982|passage=Old Turkish began with the separation, formation and consolidation of the independent '''Turkish''' languages.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Turcology in Turkey: selected papers|page=458|author=László Károly|year=2007|passage=This is openly a characteristics of Chaghatay and other Eastern '''Turkish''' languages and dialects.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|title=Hammer and Anvil|author=Pamela Kyle Crossley|passage=In the Timurid empire, the Chaghatay '''Turkish''' language, which became the standard of the Timurid court, was part of the eastern branch of Turkic languages.}}

